      "message": "Dang.. no official Meson WrapDB for OpenSSL 3.5.x.\n\nhttps://mesonbuild.com/Wrapdb-projects.html\n\n```\nopenssl\n 3.0.10-1\n3.0.8-3, 3.0.7-2, 3.0.2-1, 1.1.1l-3, 1.1.1k-2\n\n libcrypto, libssl, openssl\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/issues/323  is related.. What do folks think we should do here ?\n\nI think either 1) keep OpenSSL 3.5 mandatory \nor something like \n```\n\n// Mozilla recommended groups v6.0 where supported.\n#if OPENSSL_VERSION_PREREQ(3, 5)\n    constexpr std::string_view groups \u003d\n        \"X25519MLKEM768:X25519:prime256v1:secp384r1\";\n#else\n    constexpr std::string_view groups \u003d\n        \"X25519:prime256v1:secp384r1\";\n#endif\n\n```",
